name=Photon Sword
id=PhotonSword
description=A battery-powered, two-handed energy blade. Find a hilt (rare in sword displays, melee weapon stashes, and junk crates), fit a photon crystal (Add Weapon Upgrade, like a gun's scope) and right-click to Insert Battery, then Ignite. A lit blade hums, glows in its crystal's color, never gets bloody, and drains its battery until it switches itself off.
description=<LINE><LINE>Hotkeys (rebind in Options > Mods > Photon Sword):
description=<LINE>Z: Ignite / Extinguish (draws your sword if your hands are empty)
description=<LINE>R: Swap Battery (R still reloads guns and sharpens blades)
description=<LINE>X: Toggle Cutting while a lit blade is held (off by default; X still racks guns)
description=<LINE><LINE>An ignited sword gets its own stance: a low one-handed rest and walk, and a two-handed ready stance when aiming that now and then beckons. Aiming in the ready stance deflects bullets back at the shooter and soaks part of a shotgun blast, and blocks other photon swords' strikes, better with Long Blade skill. Running or sprinting puts the blade out until you stop.
description=<LINE><LINE>With cutting on, swings cut doors, windows, walls, objects, and vegetation, as far as the Photon Sword sandbox options allow. Cut Effect chooses Destroy or Set on Fire. Mod options set the blade light, hum, swing and hit sounds, the beckon, deflect feedback, and can switch the stance back to the game's two-handed animations.
description=<LINE><LINE>Photon Sword Forms adds fighting styles built on Senator's Martial Arms. Patch mods bring Project A-Life and Bandits NPCs who carry photon swords, and let your guard deflect their gunfire and block their swords. Removing the mod from a save deletes any Photon Swords in it. MIT licensed.
